WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.333
Welcome to the Culture Dig course,

00:00:02.333 --> 00:00:06.589
one of the three courses toward
Mosaic Practitioner Certified.

00:00:06.589 --> 00:00:10.775
You met Culture Dig, one of the
Mosaic tools developed by Dr.

00:00:10.775 --> 00:00:14.344
Chris Cancialosi, in the
Mosaic Practitioner course.

00:00:14.344 --> 00:00:19.834
This course takes you from knowing how it
works to running a whole program well:

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:25.256
buying the right thing, setting up people
so nobody sees more than they should,

00:00:25.256 --> 00:00:30.060
designing fieldwork and story collection
that produce usable evidence,

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:33.766
and turning both streams into
a report you can defend.

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:37.747
Six modules and a practical
task, about four hours in all.

00:00:38.233 --> 00:00:43.268
You already know what a Culture Dig is:
seven research teams, one story link,

00:00:43.268 --> 00:00:46.668
and two streams of evidence
read against each other.

00:00:46.668 --> 00:00:49.087
So why a whole course on running one?

00:00:49.087 --> 00:00:51.833
Because the hard parts aren't the buttons.

00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:54.056
They're the decisions around them.

00:00:54.056 --> 00:00:58.632
Who should be a Program Lead, and
who must not see the raw interviews.

00:00:58.632 --> 00:01:02.424
Whether a domain will end up
with enough stories to score.

00:01:02.424 --> 00:01:07.066
Whether a gap between a team's
conclusion and the stories is a problem,

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:09.747
or the most useful finding in the report.

00:01:09.747 --> 00:01:14.324
We'll follow one program from start
to finish: Northwind Health's dig,

00:01:14.324 --> 00:01:16.874
which you planned in the Mosaic course.

00:01:16.874 --> 00:01:19.620
By the end, you'll plan a dig of your own,

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:23.739
and write the synthesis memo a
program lead owes their sponsor.

00:01:24.233 --> 00:01:28.261
Here's how this course builds on
Module 7 of the Mosaic course.

00:01:28.261 --> 00:01:33.567
You learned the four ways to get a license;
now you'll learn what each one actually

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:34.014
grants.

00:01:34.014 --> 00:01:39.320
You learned the four roles; now you'll see
how Culture Dig really decides someone's

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.749
access, including organization admins.

00:01:41.749 --> 00:01:46.544
You learned how to log an observation
and approve a prompt; now you'll plan

00:01:46.544 --> 00:01:50.827
fieldwork, review prompts, and
watch coverage while stories arrive.

00:01:50.827 --> 00:01:55.941
And you learned the composite; now you'll
use the report's own test for where to

00:01:55.941 --> 00:01:59.265
start, and edit the draft
into something you'd sign.

00:01:59.265 --> 00:02:02.973
If you want depth on designing
story surveys from scratch,

00:02:02.973 --> 00:02:07.832
that's the Mosaic Signal course, the
third course toward your certification.

00:02:08.333 --> 00:02:13.855
This course counts toward one certification,
Mosaic Practitioner Certified,

00:02:13.855 --> 00:02:18.567
together with the Mosaic Practitioner
and Mosaic Signal courses.

00:02:18.567 --> 00:02:23.427
Here, you'll pass a short check at
the end of each content module,

00:02:23.427 --> 00:02:27.623
with a pass mark of eighty
percent and unlimited retakes,

00:02:27.623 --> 00:02:30.936
and a thirty-question
final exam, open notes,

00:02:30.936 --> 00:02:35.649
where you need eighty percent and
every critical question right.

00:02:35.649 --> 00:02:38.520
Passing the exam completes this course.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:43.747
Your practical task, a program and
fieldwork plan and a synthesis memo,

00:02:43.747 --> 00:02:45.883
is task two of your capstone.

00:02:45.883 --> 00:02:46.103
Dr.

00:02:46.103 --> 00:02:49.343
Chris Cancialosi scores
it against a rubric.

00:02:49.343 --> 00:02:51.331
There's no video to record.

00:02:51.833 --> 00:02:55.347
You know Northwind Health
from the Mosaic course.

00:02:55.347 --> 00:03:00.224
Its October Culture Progress Monitor
showed Collaboration improving,

00:03:00.224 --> 00:03:06.104
Empowered Teams flat, and a steady comment
theme: decisions made without frontline

00:03:06.104 --> 00:03:06.534
input.

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:12.199
Then, early in 2027, a Mosaic Signal
study showed how decisions land: shaped by

00:03:12.199 --> 00:03:15.570
data and deadlines, and
heard about afterwards.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:18.510
So Alex Moreau, the Chief People Officer,

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:22.526
asked the deeper question:
why do decisions feel closed,

00:03:22.526 --> 00:03:25.466
even where we think we've explained them?

00:03:25.466 --> 00:03:29.697
So Northwind ran a Culture Dig,
using the plan you drafted.

00:03:29.697 --> 00:03:32.494
They bought it on the website in March.

00:03:32.494 --> 00:03:37.872
Alex led it, with Jamie Ortiz, Northwind's
organizational development lead,

00:03:37.872 --> 00:03:38.948
as second lead.

00:03:38.948 --> 00:03:43.537
Twenty-one researchers did the
fieldwork from April the twelfth,

00:03:43.537 --> 00:03:48.342
stories came in from April the
twenty-sixth to May the seventeenth,

00:03:48.342 --> 00:03:51.641
and the report went final
on June the seventh.

00:03:51.641 --> 00:03:55.441
Each module picks the dig
up at the point it teaches.

00:03:55.933 --> 00:03:58.977
In Northwind's dig,
you're the Facilitator.

00:03:58.977 --> 00:04:02.092
You read everything,
and you change nothing.

00:04:02.092 --> 00:04:06.198
You advise Northwind under a
separate agreement with them.

00:04:06.198 --> 00:04:12.074
One thing to keep straight with every
client: a website purchase buys the software,

00:04:12.074 --> 00:04:13.277
not facilitation.

00:04:13.277 --> 00:04:16.179
No Mosaic facilitator time comes with it.

00:04:16.179 --> 00:04:21.559
Be clear about who is doing what, and
never imply the purchase included you.

00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:27.129
Before we start, think of an organization
where you might run or advise a dig in

00:04:27.129 --> 00:04:28.014
the next year.

00:04:28.014 --> 00:04:32.507
Who there would expect to see the
raw interview notes, and should they?

00:04:32.507 --> 00:04:36.556
And which domain will people find
hardest to tell a story about?

00:04:36.556 --> 00:04:37.569
Keep your notes.

00:04:37.569 --> 00:04:39.151
You'll come back to them.

00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:43.562
Two habits run through every
module: least privilege,

00:04:43.562 --> 00:04:46.943
and saying no more than
the evidence supports.

00:04:46.943 --> 00:04:49.515
Next, licenses, programs and waves.

